you can get some exercise and support  people living with bleeding disorders  here in nevada the bike senior blood  fundraiser is happening next weekend  the ride benefits the nevada chapter of  the national hemophilia foundation  we spoke to gio pernuti who's become an  avid cyclist he was born with hemophilia  and suffered a lot of injuries growing  up  i had had so many injuries and bleeds  into  my right ankle that i developed  arthritis really bad arthritis  to the point where there was like no  cartilage left in my ankle so it's bone  on bone  yeah how painful he said he could barely  get up a flight of stairs  so he had ankle fusion surgery and was  able to pick up cycling  since then he has done 20 mile marathons  he's even done a duathlon  it's kind of like my outlet if that  makes sense  i'm able to get out on the road whenever  i really want to  and just kind of concentrate on that one  thing you kind of leave  all your other problems behind so the  fundraiser is coming up next saturday  the 21st  it is virtual this year so you can bike  anywhere even on a stationary bike in  your house or a gym  proceeds benefit the local chapter and  there's some cool swag you get too so  we'll put a link  it is on our website right now it's  8newsnow.com
 

